about:
Consuelo is currently part of the Ernst & Young's Indirect Tax practice, based in Madrid (Spain) where she started her career in 2005.

From May 2013 through April 2017, she worked for Ernst & Young LLP,  where she developed her career as part of the US VAT practice, based in Chicago.

Consuelo has a wide experience on providing VAT advisory services for large multinational companies facing VAT issues worldwide, and with experience in a variety of industries. 
This includes extensive experience with the coordination of international projects of indirect taxation, such as supply chain reorganizations, and ERP system implementations, covering both European and non-European countries. 

On ERP system implementations, she has coordinated several projects involving European, LATAM and APAC countries, providing assistance with setting up the VAT determination logic;  VAT reporting functionality;  local system requirements; testing and project management.

As part of the Indirect tax practice in Ernst & Young Spain, Consuelo advises national and international companies on several VAT matters related to transactions performed within Spain.  In particular, she provides assistance with: 

•	Supply chain restructuring and other cross-border transactions;
•	Research and preparation of professional opinions concerning VAT issues;
•	VAT audits carried out by the Spanish Tax Authorities;
•	Tax controversy;
•	Spanish VAT compliance and reporting (including the review of information and VAT books prepared by clients, as well as the preparation and submission of VAT returns);
•	Coordination with the preparation and filing of VAT returns and reports, as well as supervision of the fulfillment of VAT formal obligations by Spanish companies having operations in other countries;
•	VAT refund applications.

Consuelo obtained her Economics degree in 2004. She also has a  one-year Master degree in Tax Advisory at CEF Business School in Madrid (Spain).

